WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.640
- I mean, coming from Europe

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:04.350
as an Irishman living
in London many years,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.160
Eurovision Song Contest
was a big event on TV

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.300
and remains so.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.350
So it's all the European countries

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:17.550
and they show their greatest
and finest singing acts

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.440
and they're quite
outrageous, some of them,

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.200
they really go for it,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.390
and it's very humorous
but it's very sincere

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.700
and it's very real

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.260
and it's very important
to all the countries

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.580
and it's taken to heart

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.550
and practically, you know,
all the countries of Europe,

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.900
they all close down when
the show comes on TV.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.900
And, of course, you know Abba
is one of their finest acts

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.330
that, you know, lit up the world.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.340
And I remember when they won

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:53.340
and so Abba seems to have
played a part in my life

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.300
having done two movies-

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.400
- I know, I was gonna say, I
saw "Mamma Mia", I loved it.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.780
I loved every actor in it,

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.967
it's literally like they were like,

00:01:00.967 --> 00:01:02.380
"So what actors do you wanna see

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.670
in a film together that you love?"

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.090
And then "Mamma Mia" enters.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.850
It's literally, all
you guys, I love Meryl,

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.319
I love the whole cast.

00:01:10.319 --> 00:01:11.930
Was that a really cool thing?

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.550
Like, did you always sing,

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.700
was that, like, did you sing
in front of audiences before?

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.770
- No, I mean I sang when
I was at drama school.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.720
You had to sing, you had to do everything

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:23.800
when you're a student

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:28.430
but no, I made a film,
one of my little films

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:30.863
with my company, Irish
Dreamtime, I did sing in that,

00:01:30.863 --> 00:01:34.063
it's a movie called "Evelyn"
which is a beautiful film,

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.380
but I sang Irish pub songs.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.630
It's a lot different than singing in Abba

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:44.020
and singing, you know, a
warhorse song like "S.O.S.".

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.440
So it was mildly terrifying

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.570
(Kelly laughing)
and they didn't employ me

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:51.840
for my singing talents.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.810
It was, you know, it was rough and ready

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.200
but I think it was played with such heart

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.660
and such sincerity, the whole film.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.710
- [Kelly] I loved it.

